desc: Daisy Bell (SAM, Klatt (rsynth) and Flite port) by chmaha
tags: instrument speech text-to-speech
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  A text-to-speech instrument driven entirely by MIDI text meta events
  Three engines:
  SAM: Software Automatic Mouth by Don't Ask Software (1982), ported from Sebastian Macke's
  reverse-engineered C version (https://github.com/s-macke/SAM). The SAM code has never been released
  under a licence; it is included as freely circulating abandonware and will be removed at the rightful
  owner's request.
  Klatt: the Klatt formant synthesizer from rsynth by Nick Ing-Simmons, whose README describes its parts
  as (he believed) in the public domain.
  HAL: a modified version of Flite (CMU Festival Lite) and its cmu_us_kal voice, Copyright (c) 1999-2017
  Language Technologies Institute, Carnegie Mellon University, BSD-like licence
  (see Dependencies/DaisyBell/Flite-LICENSE.txt).
  JSFX code released under AGPLv3+ license (this covers chmaha's code and the Flite port, not SAM or rsynth)
  Claude generated some of this code
provides:
  Dependencies/DaisyBell/DaisyBell-HAL.wav
  Dependencies/DaisyBell/Flite-LICENSE.txt
